xˆ32 + xˆ26 + xˆ23 + xˆ22 + xˆ16 + xˆ12 +
     xˆ11 + xˆ10 + xˆ8 + xˆ7 + xˆ5 + xˆ4 + xˆ2 + x + 1 Mathemati‐
cally, the value corresponding to a given file is defined by  the
following  procedure:  The bits to be evaluated are considered to
be the coefficients of a mod 2 polynomial M(x)  of  degree  These
bits  are  the  bits from the file, with the most significant bit
being the most significant bit of the first octet of the file and
the last bit being the least significant bit of the  last  octet,
padded  with zero bits (if necessary) to achieve an integral num‐
ber of octets, followed by one or more  octets  representing  the
length  of  the  file  as a binary value, least significant octet
first.  The smallest number of  octets  capable  of  representing
this integer are used.  M(x) is multiplied by xˆ32 (i.e., shifted
left 32 bits) and divided by G(x) using mod 2 division, producing
a  remainder  R(x)  of  degree  31.  The coefficients of R(x) are
considered to be a 32‐bit sequence.  The bit sequence is  comple‐
mented  and  the  result is the CRC.  The and utilities exit 0 on
success, and >0 if an error occurs.  The default  calculation  is
